{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"28f23b1c29684f7fc0c9a8fbac0f084a278c7745ea5c81d8b9d662fe9a127da6","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review plan-relation-snapshot reducer","key_entities":["plan-relation-snapshot-error","reducer-error","rebar review-plan",".tickets-tracker","CREATE event","SNAPSHOT event","_store/event_append._prepare_event","os.makedirs","PlanRelationSnapshotError"],"problem_keywords":["plan-relation reducer","event-less directory","indeterminate verdict","orphan ticket directory","plan review failure","store artifact"],"propositions":["A ticket directory with no CREATE or SNAPSHOT event causes the plan-relation reducer to fail, surfacing as an INDETERMINATE verdict on plan reviews of unrelated tickets.","Empty ticket directories are created by writer process death (crash/kill/timeout) between makedirs and atomic rename, and persist invisibly because git cannot track empty directories.","The plan-relation reducer walks the store directory listing and errors when encountering an event-less directory, rather than skipping it with a warning.","The reducer must tolerate event-less directories by skipping them and naming the path in a warning, without silently dropping genuinely corrupt tickets that hold events but fail to reduce."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787772440149442001,"uuid":"46cf7104-deaa-4f67-a736-5bc5ecb46533"}